# The deploy target's SSH host key, pinned so CI does not trust-on-first-use a
# key it has no way to check. Copied from a workstation that already had the
# host in its own known_hosts, and verified to match:
#
#   256 SHA256:TdponGy4FJg6Dlpl8j9DALnB3hpStTsjESyYYVNvsMQ (ED25519)
#
# If the server is ever rebuilt, the deploy fails loudly with a host-key
# mismatch — which is the point. Refresh it deliberately, from a machine that
# already trusts the new host:
#
#   ssh-keyscan -t ed25519 p9.fhnw-rover.ch >> deploy/known_hosts
#
# Both names are the same box and the same key. deploy.sh derives the target
# from site.config.json, so it connects as p9.fhnw-rover.ch; the old name is
# kept so an older checkout still verifies against this file.
p9.fhnw-rover.ch ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIJ+2RjtRj88LXL3lDq3ctOq3+raBACQ4PhKMjMdxbbhQ
p9.fhnw-rover.sacovo.ch ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIJ+2RjtRj88LXL3lDq3ctOq3+raBACQ4PhKMjMdxbbhQ
